      "role": "user",
      "content": "Right, I get the \"inclusive governance\" part, but let's be real for a second. In these types of multi-ethnic West African settings, isn't there usually a much higher baseline risk for ethnic conflict or tribalism compared to more homogenous regions? I'm trying to figure out if we should bake in a \"conflict premium\" for our ROI models because of how these groups traditionally interact over resources.",
