      "content": "That makes sense. Just to drill down on that 'heightened risk' you mentioned—are you saying that the very nature of having these traditional ethnic divisions in a multi-ethnic state makes conflict almost inevitable over time? Like, do these societies have an inherent difficulty maintaining a centralized state compared to Western-style nation-states where identity is more unified? I'm trying to understand if the volatility is just a baked-in characteristic of these regions.",
